        "content": {
          "kind": "html",
          "value": "<div style='width:100%;height:100%;overflow:auto;box-sizing:border-box;container-type:inline-size;background:#ffffff;font-family:Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#0f172a'><div style='box-sizing:border-box;max-width:900px;margin:0 auto;padding:0 clamp(20px,5cqw,40px) 64px'><div style='padding-top:32px'><header data-role='masthead'><div style='padding:10px 0;border-top:3px solid #0f172a;border-bottom:1px solid #0f172a;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6d28d9'>PRIMITIVE · edge</div><h1 style='margin:40px 0 0;font:500 clamp(40px,9.5cqw,72px)/.98 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;letter-spacing:-.025em;text-wrap:balance;color:#0f172a'>Edge</h1><p style='margin:18px 0 0;max-width:36ch;font:italic 400 clamp(20px,3.6cqw,26px)/1.35 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#475569'>One relationship between two endpoints in a graph.</p></header></div><div style='padding-top:48px'><div style='display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:flex-start;gap:32px 40px'><div style='flex:999 1 380px;min-width:0'><section data-role='section'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6d28d9'>Meaning</h2><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#1e293b'><span style='float:left;padding:6px 10px 0 0;font:500 68px/54px Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#0f172a'>A</span> relationship instance joining graph endpoints. Encoding: an entry in the graph’s edges array, not a node. Its meaning comes from the relationship/Edge Class, not its drawn curve.</p></section></div><div style='flex:1 1 220px;min-width:0'><section data-role='settings' style='padding-top:10px;border-top:3px solid #0f172a'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#0f172a'>At a glance</h2><dl style='margin:0;display:grid;grid-template-columns:max-content 1fr;column-gap:12px;border-bottom:1px solid #cbd5e1'><dt style='grid-column:1/-1;padding:9px 0 0px;border-top:1px solid #cbd5e1;font:400 13px/20px system-ui;color:#475569'>Encoded as</dt><dd style='grid-column:1/-1;margin:0;padding:2px 0 9px;font:600 14px/20px system-ui;color:#0f172a;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>an entry in the graph’s edges array, not a node</dd></dl></section></div></div></div><div style='padding-top:48px'><section data-role='section'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6d28d9'>Invariants</h2><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#1e293b'>Endpoint identities survive layout changes. Routing pins and lane geometry do not change semantic endpoints. Cross-graph ownership must be persisted with the owning graphs, not only in a workspace drawing.</p></section></div><div style='padding-top:48px'><section data-role='section'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6d28d9'>Contract</h2><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#1e293b'>An edge records id, source, target, sourcePort/targetPort, type and data. Its <code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#f1f5f9;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>type</code> is its kind: the key of its class, or <code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#f1f5f9;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>edge</code> for an edge with no class. <code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#f1f5f9;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>data.classRef</code> names the class graph. An edge is called a link when it is on the web: a hyperlink from one graph to another. Edge label and style are not substitutes for connection rules.</p></section></div><div style='padding-top:48px'><section data-role='section'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6d28d9'>Ports and Relationships</h2><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#1e293b'>Connects declared sockets of nodes, including graph Ports. Surface exposure and next-face are concrete relationship types; a relationship’s allowed source/target kinds and cardinality come from its class.</p></section></div><div style='padding-top:48px'><section data-role='section'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6d28d9'>Behavior</h2><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#1e293b'>edgeLegality resolves the class key, checks kinds and counts matching incoming/outgoing relationships. The graph validator diagnoses loaded invalid relationships, and mutation paths can reject illegal new edges. Intergraph edge references preserve ownership on the participating graphs’ roots.</p></section></div><div style='padding-top:48px'><section data-role='section'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6d28d9'>Known gaps</h2><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#1e293b'>Before default edge classes load there may be no rule to apply. This is registry availability, not proof that any authored relationship is valid. Browser reconnect/drag behavior requires its own smoke test.</p></section></div><div style='padding-top:48px'><section data-role='section'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6d28d9'>Representations</h2><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#1e293b'>Edges draw as routes between handles, with labels and optional strokes. Layout decoration is independent of graph meaning.</p></section></div><div style='padding-top:48px'><section data-role='section'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6d28d9'>Explicitly Not Part of This Primitive</h2><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#1e293b'>Not a node type, not an Edge Class definition, and not a semantic router merely because its route has pins.</p></section></div><div style='padding-top:48px'><section data-role='section'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6d28d9'>Examples</h2><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#1e293b'>No example graph is linked from this page yet.</p></section></div><div style='padding-top:48px'><section data-role='section'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6d28d9'>Where this lives</h2><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#1e293b'>Source (twilite repository):</p><ul style='margin:0 0 14px;padding-left:22px;max-width:60ch;font:400 18px/1.55 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#1e293b'><li style='margin:0 0 6px'><code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#f1f5f9;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>components/GraphEditor/utils/edgeLegality.js</code></li><li style='margin:0 0 6px'><code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#f1f5f9;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>components/GraphEditor/utils/interGraphEdge.js</code></li><li style='margin:0 0 6px'><code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#f1f5f9;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>components/GraphEditor/validators/validateGraphInvariants.js</code></li></ul><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#1e293b'>Focused tests (twilite repository):</p><ul style='margin:0 0 14px;padding-left:22px;max-width:60ch;font:400 18px/1.55 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#1e293b'><li style='margin:0 0 6px'><code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#f1f5f9;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>tests/edgeLegality.test.js</code></li><li style='margin:0 0 6px'><code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#f1f5f9;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>tests/edgeEndpointResolution.test.js</code></li><li style='margin:0 0 6px'><code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#f1f5f9;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>tests/interGraphEdge.test.js</code></li></ul><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#1e293b'>These pointers identify evidence to inspect. Structural validation does not prove runtime or browser behavior.</p></section></div></div></div>"
        },
